The "this game is now pointless" aspect of an
accidental conversion prior to the Quest has always
seemed a bit empty and cold.

How about instead of just "quit, die, or escape" a
"consolation prize quest" be added for this corner
case, or perhaps even one such quest for each role,
or a smaller or larger assortment of randomly chosen
such quests, where the PC can't get to the amulet of
Yendor, but can fill hir arms with goodies to take
back to the village from which s/he originated?

Something like an infinitely invokable Horn of
Plenty, a wheel that spun wool into gold, the hammer
of Vulcan for the town's smith/forge, a gander whose
fertilizing caused golden eggs, a biddable basilisk
to guard the village gate, or similar frippery would
seem appropriate, and I'm sure lots of other quest
not-quite-artifacts could be imagined, that would
find the returning PC hailed as something less than
a dunce.

[Dying further on and leaving this prize in a bones
file would find the _player_ hailed, or perhaps
cursed, by the bones file recipient.]

The Quest Leader, when the "wrong deity" PC
approached, would give some avuncular advice, point
to an until then unnoticed portal/closet, give the
PC a "two steps" running start, and then sic the
minions/guards after hir. Guards that were next to
the PC at the closet door when the PC triggered the
portal would follow in pursuit through the portal,
too. The return to the main dungeon would be by
using the portal at the other end, bypassing the
Quest home level and its hornets' nest of minions.

The "consolation quest branch" could be structured
much like the main quest branch, and easier, equally
difficult, or harder as the patch writer chose. I
perceive the consolation-Quest leader as an oily
sort well willing to send the converted PC to a
gloriously gruesome death in the name of the new
deity.

Put _enough_ extra, random consolation quest levels
and acquisitions in place and this could become a
rich new "alternate objective" addition to NetHack.

A really vindictive PC, if successful and surviving
in the consolation quest could once more enter the
main Quest portal to clear the Quest home level of
all living beings, later, if desired.

xanthian, looking for a "pudding farm" consolation
quest with a suitably spherical quest leader.

"Tell me 'you're not good enough' will you?"




